package fixedwait

// Entry is one function's counted references that the series has not yet
// removed, by the category the survey gave each one.
//
// KEYED BY FUNCTION, NOT BY LINE, so an unrelated edit above a wait never
// churns the table, and COUNTED BY SHAPE — the fixed waits ([Entry.Waits])
// apart from the readings of elapsed time ([Entry.Readings]) — so a new wait
// added beside an old one in the same function still fails the gate, and so
// does a reading added where a removed wait was.
type Entry struct {
	// File is the path from the module's root, slash-separated.
	File string
	// Func is the enclosing top-level declaration as [Ref.Func] names it:
	// a function's name, a method's as Type.Method.
	Func string

	// The deciding categories of a fixed wait, the class's first three
	// shapes.
	NegativeWindow   int
	HeadStart        int
	PositiveDeadline int
	// ClockStep: the wait only moves the wall clock past an instant the
	// code under test stamped, so that a later stamp differs. It is in the
	// class, since the verdict depends on wall-clock time having passed,
	// though it cannot flake, and no marker takes it out: its fix is a
	// clock the test controls (internal/clocktest, or a Now the code under
	// test is handed), which removes the wait.
	ClockStep int
	// ExemptWait: the survey read the wait and it decides nothing on the
	// wall clock. The piece that owns it adds the marker, choosing the
	// kind, and re-reads it first: one that turns out to decide a claim is
	// fixed like the deciding ones.
	ExemptWait int

	// ElapsedBound: the fourth shape, a positive deadline whose clock is
	// READ rather than waited on — time.Since, time.Until, or a
	// time.Time's Sub, Before, After or Compare held to a bound, an
	// ordering of two instants the code stamped from the wall clock among
	// them — which fails a healthy build when a loaded runner loses time
	// between the two readings. Its fix is #736's: the instant a wait was
	// armed with, held exactly, where a fake sees the wait; the bubble's
	// answer instant where none does; otherwise the signal the bound stood
	// in for; and for an ordering of two stamps, the order the code
	// records.
	ElapsedBound int
	// ExemptElapsed: the survey read the reading of elapsed time and it
	// decides nothing on the wall clock — logged, reported, a poll's own
	// deadline (measure), or a comparison of instants no wall clock
	// separates (stated). Its piece marks it, re-reading it first, as
	// ExemptWait's does.
	ExemptElapsed int

	// Piece is the number of the series' pull request that removes the
	// entry, in crewlet/crewlet#734's list.
	Piece int
}

// Waits is the fixed waits the entry records, which the gate holds to the
// function's waits alone.
func (e Entry) Waits() int {
	return e.NegativeWindow + e.HeadStart + e.PositiveDeadline + e.ClockStep + e.ExemptWait
}

// Readings is the readings of elapsed time the entry records, which the gate
// holds to the function's readings alone: a reading never stands in for a
// wait the piece removed, nor a wait for a reading.
func (e Entry) Readings() int { return e.ElapsedBound + e.ExemptElapsed }

// Total is every reference the entry records.
func (e Entry) Total() int { return e.Waits() + e.Readings() }

// allowed is every function whose fixed waits and readings of elapsed time
// the series has yet to remove.
//
// ADDING AN ENTRY IS THE DECISION, and no piece of the series adds one: the
// table only shrinks. A piece that fixes a function's references lowers or
// removes its entry in the same diff, and the gate fails an entry that
// records more than its function holds, so a fix cannot leave its entry
// behind. A new wait or reading is decided by one of the house patterns or
// marked, in the package doc.
